{
  "version": 287,
  "released": "2026-09-03",
  "changelog": "v287: TIMELINE UNIFICATION 6a \u2014 ADD LANDMARK, THE `offer` MODE OF THE LANDMARKS INTERACTION. Until this release the Landmarks Interaction only asked. The system chose a domain, asked the next rung, and the recorder filed the answer; everything about the lane assumed the system started the conversation. A person arriving holding a whole run of addresses, or a work history, or one paragraph about the year they moved, had exactly one door: a paste page behind a strict `Key: value` grammar whose every failure \u2014 a malformed date, an expired token, a network drop \u2014 arrived as one sentence, \"Could not parse that paste right now.\" The owner's ruling of 2026-09-03 (decision record R3/R3a/R3b): \"A parser is probably too strict\", and the product built around it \"never achieved its goal. Add Landmark is what I wanted.\"\n\nNew: `system/landmark_offer.py`, `interactions/landmarks/prompt/turn-instructions-offer.md`, `docs/adr/0033-add-landmark-offer-mode.md`, `interactions/landmarks/evals/goldens/offer_fixtures.json`, `tests/test_landmark_offer.py`. `interaction.yaml` declares `modes: collect|offer` and a third composition slot beside the recorder's and the listener's; `interactions/registry.json` is UNTOUCHED. It is a MODE, not an interaction kind (R3b), and it composes no new extractor: the general listener (ADR 0029) reads the text with no domain, the focused recorder (ADR 0028) reads it once per domain the listener named with that domain's filed entries in view \u2014 which is what makes a second stay in a known city a second entry rather than a merge \u2014 and a deterministic block grammar runs first over text it fully matches, so a thirty-block residence document proposes thirty units for the cost of a string split. A block with one line the grammar does not know is not half-parsed; it goes to the listener whole.\n\nSTATED VERSUS INFERRED IS DECIDED FROM THE BYTES (decision record \u00a74.2). `landmark_offer.date_evidence` re-reads every bound of every proposed date against the person's own text \u2014 the year in full (`1990`) or in the two-digit form people write (`'91`), and a finer grain with its month named. A bound the text carries files `basis: stated`; a bound it does not carries `confidence: inferred` and a verbatim inferred provenance clause, WHATEVER the completion declared. The model that guessed the year is the last thing that should grade the guess.\n\nNOTHING FILES BEFORE A PERSON CONFIRMS, AND NOTHING IS LOST IF THEY DO NOT. `propose` writes exactly one file \u2014 `state/landmarks/offers/<proposal_id>.json`, newly registered in `vault_contract.json` \u2014 carrying the submitted text, the units with their quotes and offsets, the stories, the spans nothing recognized, and the open questions. It writes it on failure too. `apply` files the units the person named through `timeline.save_landmark`, the ONE landmark writer, so a confirmed offer and an answered question are indistinguishable downstream; identity is `(proposal_id, unit_id)` through the existing `digest_override` seam, never a filing ordinal, so a retry files nothing twice and returns the standing receipt. The receipt carries Cut 4c's realized-gain sentence. `retract` files a durable retraction over exactly the claims the filed units stand on \u2014 found by the promoted source each unit wrote, so undoing the second stay at an address never touches the first \u2014 and republishes; the evidence and the receipt stay on disk and the retraction is its own immutable file beside them.\n\nNOTHING IS DROPPED AND NOTHING IS REFUSED. Every span of a submission ends up under exactly one of a unit's quote, `stories` or `unrecognized`, and a lint asserts the three cover the text between them. Non-landmark text is accepted, routed as a story, and said so (R3a) \u2014 \"I could not use that\" is the one sentence the offer turn may never contain.\n\nThe manifest gains three deterministic context blocks (\u00a75.2) \u2014 the roster with its aliases, the published projection's episodes and eras with their spans, and the age frames with the birth origin they are counted from \u2014 rendered by `landmarks_interaction.render_roster` / `render_known_spans` / `render_age_frames`, pure functions beside `render_known_entries`. The model interprets; it does not fetch. New verb: `lifehug.py landmark-offer --propose|--apply|--retract`, classified by name as a vault mutation because `--propose` writes the person's own words to disk. A filed unit retires its matching Cut 5a opportunity by CLOSING THE GAP rather than by setting a flag: `apply` reads the published `landmark_opportunities` block either side of the filing and reports on the receipt which of the unit's candidate ids actually closed, and `landmark_offer.landmark_opportunity_id` is a named door onto `landmark_opportunities.opportunity_id`, never a second digest. Evals: five goldens, one per example in decision record \u00a75.6, replayed through the real `propose` with recorded completions, and four `landmark_offer_gates.*` gates at 1.0.",
